WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.500
OK.

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.400
A lot of questions are also coming in about
the debates.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.340
Three debates have been agreed to in principle
between Joe Biden and Donald Trump.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.790
Don't yet know when they will be, where they
will be.

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:11.900
Will there be an audience?

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:18.390
I don't have the details yet, but the question
I'm getting from a lot of people is essentially

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:22.050
how can we expect Biden to do in debates against
Trump?

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:28.160
A lot of right wingers are saying Trump, Biden,
dementia, Biden can't put together a sentence.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:33.090
So let's put aside the hot takes about Biden
can't speak.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:35.910
He's completely demented at this point.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:43.219
I think that what we have to understand is,
first of all, historically, our expectations

00:00:43.219 --> 00:00:49.309
about this debate is going to destroy this
candidate or that candidate.

00:00:49.309 --> 00:00:52.930
That happens very rarely in high level politics
in the United States.

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:59.149
From my perspective, Donald Trump so thoroughly
embarrassed himself against Hillary Clinton

00:00:59.149 --> 00:01:01.390
in the debates in 2016.

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:05.059
The debates did not move the needle particularly.

00:01:05.059 --> 00:01:10.689
And Trump ended up winning, as we all know,
when the Democratic primary just a few months

00:01:10.689 --> 00:01:11.950
ago feels like years ago.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:16.729
But it was a few months ago when the Democratic
primary this year got down to Bernie versus

00:01:16.729 --> 00:01:17.799
Biden.

00:01:17.799 --> 00:01:23.140
You had the same Biden dementia people saying
as soon as Bernie gets a shot against Biden,

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:26.600
one on one, Bernie's going to Russia.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:29.150
Biden is not going to be able to take it.

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:31.550
And Biden did fine in that debate.

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:35.189
Now, there are people who said after the fact,
well, it was because the moderators helped

00:01:35.189 --> 00:01:40.430
Biden by making it all about Corona virus
or listen, people some people were convinced

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:44.600
there was no way Biden would even be able
to string together a sentence that was coherent.

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:49.290
Biden did fine and went on to win the primary
very, very handily.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:56.299
So if you're expecting some black swan event
where we know every once in a while a debate

00:01:56.299 --> 00:02:02.280
does change as a race drastically, you're
probably going to be disappointed.

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:09.149
I do concede, and I've been saying this for
a while, Joe Biden at 78, 77, is not the Joe

00:02:09.149 --> 00:02:13.920
Biden that debated Paul Ryan, for example,
back in 2012.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:16.370
So I believe Biden knows this.

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:18.480
I believe the people around Biden know it.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:24.550
So I would expect Biden to train for a scenario
that favors him.

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:31.830
So knowing how to get under Trump's skin without
putting himself in situations for maybe the

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:38.430
type of rapid fire that would not be playing
to his strengths at this point in time, that

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:40.950
that's certainly, you know, maybe a case.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:45.989
This has not, you know, on the on the Trump
side, people preparing him for the debate

00:02:45.989 --> 00:02:52.390
are going to be probably in a futile manner,
trying to get him to think about the debates

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:58.420
in a way where he won't end up saying something
racist or xenophobic or discriminatory or,

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:02.700
you know, I want less testing because then
we find fewer cases or whatever.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:10.489
So my vision is that the debates are likely
going to be underwhelming for anybody expecting

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:16.280
really the types of fireworks that you see
once in a blue moon that shake up a race.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:20.010
Remember, according to the polls, Trump is
going to be coming into these debates playing

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:21.220
from behind.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:24.130
But with the power of incumbency.

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:28.470
If Joe Biden can simply and this is not an
endorsement of any policy, if Joe Biden can

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:38.630
show up and present himself as the elder statesman
diplomat alongside this unhinged, wild, wacky

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:42.129
Trump doesn't have to change that many minds.

00:03:42.129 --> 00:03:45.990
That will probably be good enough for Joe
Biden to maintain his lead.

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:47.680
What else did I want?

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.849
Oh, one other thing I wanted to mention.

00:03:49.849 --> 00:03:56.250
There are people who are hoping that the debates
will be Joe Biden calling out Trump's belligerence

00:03:56.250 --> 00:04:01.129
and Trump's insane comments and Trump's comments
about women and about black people and all

00:04:01.129 --> 00:04:02.390
this different stuff.

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:03.780
It just doesn't really work that well.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:04.780
Right.

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:10.769
I mean, we've seen that it hasn't worked well
as something to hurt Trump during the campaign

00:04:10.769 --> 00:04:12.090
and during his presidency.

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:17.000
What has really hurt Trump recently has been
failure on corona virus, subsequent failure

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:23.750
on the economy, failure on his embarrassing
response to the protests against police brutality.

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:28.460
That's where Biden should focus, because we've
seen that the stuff that does just load off

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:34.160
or, you know, slide off of Trump is the stuff
about grab him by the you know what?

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:37.840
Where's my African-American tweeting the white
power video?

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:41.340
I don't think that there's really a winning
strategy there for Biden.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:44.940
I think the strategy is look at the stuff
that's gone wrong.

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:49.060
Trump trying to gut Obamacare during a pandemic.

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:50.060
Right.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:52.860
That's where the focus should be from a policy
standpoint for Joe Biden.

